                                "example_id": "cac9156e-90ee-48e4-9e20-3fe42351fff4",
                                "sense_id": "fdfeeef8-f45e-3d29-9b59-f48905702732",
                                "text": "The most exact chronologers tell us that Christ was born in October, and not in December."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bcbef165-b544-41d2-a222-70cd629cbfd6",
                                "sense_id": "fdfeeef8-f45e-3d29-9b59-f48905702732",
                                "text": "My whole contention is, in face, that we know enough, by this time, from Egyptian and other non-Hellenistic sources, to be able to assert that neigher Eusebius, nor Trogus, nor any other Hellenistic or Graeco-Roman chronologer knew anything of value about such matters as the foundation of Trapezus […]"
                            }
